 ****************************************************************  228 1451   11
                         ENDF/B-VII.1 beta                         228 1451   12
                             G.M.Hale                              228 1451   13
                               LANL                                228 1451   14
                          September 2010                           228 1451   15
                                                                   228 1451   16
The evaluation done originally by Nisley et al. in 1973 has been   228 1451   17
updated to include the results of a more recent R-matrix analysis. 228 1451   18
The 1973 analysis was based on a simultaneous fit of n-alpha and   228 1451   19
p-alpha scattering data. The newer analysis (8/06) is a multi-     228 1451   20
channel fit to data for the n-alpha and d-t reactions that extends 228 1451   21
to about 24 MeV excitation energy in the 5He system. Although this 228 1451   22
is well above the d+t threshold, for the present, we give n-alpha  228 1451   23
data only over the original range up to 20 MeV, where it is single 228 1451   24
channel scattering. However, the results below the d+t threshold   228 1451   25
are constrained by the data at higher energies through the         228 1451   26
R-matrix parameterization, and they are therefore better           228 1451   27
determined than those of a single-channel analysis.                228 1451   28
                                                                   228 1451   29
In addition, covariances (MF=33) are given for MT=2, calculated    228 1451   30
from the parameter covariances and derivatives from the 5He        228 1451   31
analysis. It should be noted that while the rank of this           228 1451   32
covariance matrix is 115, corresponding to the number of free      228 1451   33
parameters in the fit, it is given at 152 energies. This means     228 1451   34
that in principle some of the zero eigenvalues could have small    228 1451   35
negative values due to the limited precision of the numbers in the 228 1451   36
file and the matrix is not guaranteed to be positive semi-         228 1451   37
definite.                                                          228 1451   38
                                                                   228 1451   39
