 ENDF/B-V Evaluation, October 1973, R.A. Nisley, G.M. Hale,        228 1451   60
                      P.G. Young (LANL)                            228 1451   61
                                                                   228 1451   62
 MF=3 ------------ SMOOTH CROSS SECTIONS ------------------------  228 1451   63
                                                                   228 1451   64
         THE 2200 M/S CROSS SECTIONS ARE AS FOLLOWS,               228 1451   65
             MT=1   SIGMA= 0.75916 BARNS                           228 1451   66
             MT=2   SIGMA= 0.75916 BARNS                           228 1451   67
                                                                   228 1451   68
   MT=1       TOTAL CROSS SECTION                                  228 1451   69
         SEE DISCUSSION UNDER MT=2 BELOW                           228 1451   70
                                                                   228 1451   71
   MT=2       ELASTIC SCATTERING CROSS SECTION                     228 1451   72
         ALTHOUGH THE ONLY REACTION POSSIBLE FOR NEUTRONS INCIDENT 228 1451   73
       ON HE-4 BELOW 20 MEV IS ELASTIC SCATTERING, THE MAJORITY    228 1451   74
       OF THE N-4HE DATA IS RATHER IMPRECISE.  IN ORDER TO OVER-   228 1451   75
       COME THIS PROBLEM, AN R-MATRIX ANALYSIS WAS PERFORMED WITH  228 1451   76
       A DATA SET WHICH INCLUDED NOT ONLY THE N-4HE DATA BUT ALSO  228 1451   77
       VERY PRECISE P-4HE DATA.  ALL THE AVAILABLE N-4HE AND P-4HE 228 1451   78
       DATA BELOW 20 MEV WERE CONSIDERED IN THE ANALYSIS.  SINCE   228 1451   79
       THE PREVIOUS EVALUATION WAS COMPLETED IN 1968, SEVERAL      228 1451   80
       N-4HE ELASTIC SCATTERING MEASUREMENTS HAVE BEEN DONE.  THE  228 1451   81
       MOST SIGNIFICANT OF THESE ARE THE LOW ENERGY NEUTRON CROSS  228 1451   82
       SECTION OF RORER (RO69),THE RPI TOTAL CROSS SECTION         228 1451   83
       MEASUREMENT (GO73), WHICH COVER THE RANGE EN=0.7-30 MEV,    228 1451   84
       AND THE RELATIVE ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS OF MORGAN (MO68).    228 1451   85
       A COMPLETE LIST OF REFERENCES FOR THE N-4HE DATA USED IS    228 1451   86
       GIVEN BELOW.  THE P-4HE DATA WAS SELECTED TO SATISFY VERY   228 1451   87
       STRINGENT STATISTICAL CRITERIA AND WE BELIEVE THE POSSIBLE  228 1451   88
       ERRORS OF THE PREDICTED VALUES FOR THE P-4HE SCATTERING     228 1451   89
       TO BE LESS THAN 1.0 PER CENT.  A SIMPLE MODEL FOR THE       228 1451   90
       CHARGE DIFFERENCES BETWEEN THE N-4HE AND P-4HE SYSTEMS      228 1451   91
       WAS ASSUMED AND THE N-4HE AND P-4HE DATA SETS WERE          228 1451   92
       SIMULTANEOUSLY ANALYZED.  THE VALUES OF THE CROSS SECTIONS  228 1451   93
       AND ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS CONTAINED IN FILES 3 AND 4 ARE    228 1451   94
       PROBABLY ACCURATE TO WITHIN 2.0 PERCENT.                    228 1451   95
